        "heading_Yq6GFy": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A Bold, Contemporary Restaurant Concept on Mill Road, Cambridge ",
            "text_size": 4,
            "padding_bottom": 16
          }
        },
        "text_Wc4Vwb": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Maza at Eighty-Six is a new Pakistani and Indian restaurant concept located in the heart of Cambridge, designed and delivered by Simran Design from concept to completion. The brief: to create a casual, characterful space that feels modern, inclusive, and rooted in culture – appealing to students, families, and food lovers alike.</p><p>We led the full creative process – from naming and branding to interior concept, material sourcing, and final installation. Inspired by Eastern warmth with a Western edge, the space features rich textures, graphic signage, and a relaxed layout that invites guests to dine in or take away.</p><p><strong>Location:</strong> Mill Road, Cambridge<br/><strong>Scope:</strong> Full branding, restaurant concept, naming, interior design, FF&E sourcing, installation</p>",
            "text_size": 2,
            "text_style": "font-body",
            "padding_bottom": 16
          }
        },
        "heading_deKB9A": {
          "type": "heading",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "KEY FEATURES",
            "text_size": 3,
            "padding_bottom": 16
          }
        },
        "text_JLr7JP": {
          "type": "text",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "text": "<ul><li><strong>A new private call room</strong> has been introduced to support confidential conversations and focused work<br/></li><li><strong>Bespoke booth seating</strong> with integrated LED lighting, providing comfortable breakout seating while adding a subtle, atmospheric design feature<br/></li><li><strong>Acoustic design strategy</strong> incorporating wall panelling, acoustic carpeting, and ceiling-suspended baffles to enhance sound control and overall comfort within the space</li><li><strong>Open-plan office redesign</strong> to encourage collaboration while maintaining a structured, professional feel<br/></li><li><strong>Refreshed reception area and meeting room</strong> creating a strong first impression for clients and visitors<br/></li><li><strong>Conversion of an existing shower room into a secondary WC</strong>, improving staff facilities and usability<br/></li><li><strong>Bold, brand-led colour palette</strong> of black, white, and deep red applied in a refined, contemporary way</li></ul>",
            "text_size": 3,
            "text_style": "font-body",
            "padding_bottom": 16
          }
        }
      },
